From be6b8c6b1b35f6b851d662f3b7d11d8a994b8289 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 30 May 2026 15:21:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(auth): catch DioException + log API URL so Android auth
 failures are debuggable
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Symptom: every login flow on Android (Google, Facebook, email/password)
shows a generic snackbar ("Google sign-in failed", "Login failed") with
no actionable detail. The PlatformException diagnostic shipped earlier
caught google_sign_in plugin errors but missed the most likely Android
failure mode — the HTTP call from Dio to the FastAPI backend at
https://api.legacytable.app.

Root-cause hypothesis: when all three flows fail uniformly (email/password
included, which never touches Google/Facebook config), the only shared
piece is the backend HTTP request. A DioException being swallowed by the
existing catch (which checks toString().contains('Exception:'), and
DioException's toString begins with 'DioException', not 'Exception:')
explains why all three snackbars look identical and useless.

Changes:
- Add 'package:dio/dio.dart' import for DioException type.
- Add 'package:flutter/services.dart' import for PlatformException type.
- New _describeAuthError() helper formats:
    * DioException → connectionError vs badResponse vs timeout vs cert
      issue, plus the URL + status code + response body (in debugPrint).
    * PlatformException → "[code]: detail" so plugin errors stay
      visible (Google ApiException codes, etc.).
    * Anything starting with 'Exception:' → stripped prefix.
    * Anything else → toString as last resort.
  Every path also calls debugPrint with full runtimeType + value so
  'flutter logs' captures the unredacted error.
- All three catch blocks (_handleLogin email/password, _handleGoogleSignIn,
  _handleFacebookSignIn) now route through _describeAuthError().
- main.dart prints the active API base URL + isProduction flag once at
  boot, so 'flutter logs' immediately shows which backend the build is
  pointing at. (A wrong base URL is the #1 cause of universal-auth-fail
  on Android — emulator localhost gotcha, stale dev IP, etc.)

After this lands and the Android build is reinstalled, the snackbar will
say one of:
  "Google sign-in failed: can't reach https://api.legacytable.app/api.
   Check internet / VPN, or verify the backend is up."
  "Login failed: backend returned 500. {detail: ...}"
  "Google sign-in failed [sign_in_failed]: ApiException: 10:"
  ...etc — each pointing at a specific root cause to fix next.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
